Package: csemGT
Type: Package
Title: Conditional Standard Error of Measurement in Generalizability Theory
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Rene", "Gempp", email = "rene.gempp@udp.cl",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Estimates the conditional standard error of measurement
    (CSEM) within the Generalizability Theory framework for the
    persons-by-items single-facet crossed design (Brennan, 1998).
    Returns person-level CSEM estimates for absolute and relative
    error variances, with three estimators of the relative error
    variance (full, large_a, uncorrelated), closed-form analytical
    and item-resampling bootstrap sampling variances, quadratic
    smoothing of CSEMs on observed score, D-study extrapolation,
    and post-estimation plotting in base graphics. This is a focused
    release; the broader 'csemR' package, in development, will provide
    additional families of CSEM estimators (split-half, ANOVA-based,
    binomial and compound binomial). Users seeking the full suite
    should install 'csemR' once available.
